# @balancer-labs/v2-deployments and the two @uniswap packages are artifact bags: this deployer reads
# their compiled JSON off disk with readFileSync (src/protocols/balancer-v2.ts, uniswap-v3.ts) and
# never imports a line of their code. They declare `hardhat` and `@ethersproject/contracts` as peer
# dependencies, and npm 7+ installs peers automatically -- so a package with zero real dependencies
# was dragging in a whole hardhat 2.x toolchain, and with it 20 advisories (undici, uuid, adm-zip,
# @sentry/node, elliptic, the ethers v5 stack) that no code path here can reach. hardhat 2.x pins
# those versions and will not move; there is no bump that clears them.
#
# The Aave and GMX deploys DO run hardhat, but the vendored ones: `npx hardhat` is spawned with cwd
# set to vendor/<protocol>/, which resolves that tree's own hardhat. This file does not touch those.
omit=peer
